#%PAM-1.0
# buchhwin-shell lock screen, password only, on Arch Linux. lock.qml switches
# to this service when the password is submitted while pam_fprintd
# (buchhwin-lock) still waits for a finger, and when the reader is off or the
# lid is closed. Arch has no password-auth, so the password part of
# system-auth is spelled out here, pam_faillock included: system-auth counts
# wrong passwords (3, then 10 minutes locked) and refuses a locked account, and
# without the same lines here the lid-shut lock allowed unlimited guesses and
# unlocked an account system-auth had locked. The lock face shows faillock's
# messages (LockLogic.lockoutNotice). pam_systemd_home is left out, as it
# always was here.
auth       required                    pam_faillock.so  preauth
auth       [success=1 default=bad]     pam_unix.so      try_first_pass
auth       [default=die]               pam_faillock.so  authfail
auth       required                    pam_env.so
auth       required                    pam_faillock.so  authsucc
account    required                    pam_permit.so
